not really spending

00:52:17.734 --> 00:52:19.600
a whole lot of
time with the kiddos.

00:52:19.600 --> 00:52:23.667
How did you establish
that relationship later on?

00:52:24.500 --> 00:52:26.133
- Well, let me
tell you something.

00:52:26.133 --> 00:52:28.100
Looking back, and I'm sixty--

00:52:28.100 --> 00:52:29.066
How old am I?

00:52:29.066 --> 00:52:30.767
Sixty three.

00:52:30.767 --> 00:52:32.867
- That's crazy. Is that true?

00:52:32.867 --> 00:52:34.700
Yeah, you are. Holy shit.

00:52:34.700 --> 00:52:35.800
- [Sasha] Yeah, sixty-three.

00:52:35.800 --> 00:52:39.100
Looking back...
- [Gary] That's crazy.

00:52:39.100 --> 00:52:42.033
I have regrets.

00:52:43.800 --> 00:52:46.033
Luckily it's worked out for me.

00:52:46.033 --> 00:52:50.567
But I did not go to any games.

00:52:50.567 --> 00:52:55.734
Gary played baseball and
Little League and all that.

00:52:55.734 --> 00:52:57.934
I didn't go to anything.

00:52:59.133 --> 00:53:01.633
At one point in school...

00:53:03.667 --> 00:53:07.400
everybody was
under the impression...

00:53:07.400 --> 00:53:09.767
my wife does not have a husband.

00:53:11.033 --> 00:53:11.867
That's true.

00:53:11.867 --> 00:53:15.033
- [Gary] Yeah.
- Okay?

00:53:15.033 --> 00:53:17.934
People were talking
about and saying she made up

00:53:17.934 --> 00:53:20.300
she had a husband or something.

00:53:20.300 --> 00:53:22.100
Because I work every hour.

00:53:22.100 --> 00:53:25.533
And, you know
what, looking back...

00:53:25.533 --> 00:53:29.033
again luckily for me,
for the family,

00:53:29.033 --> 00:53:30.567
things worked out with the kids,

00:53:30.567 --> 00:53:33.233
but I have a lot of regrets.

00:53:33.233 --> 00:53:37.400
What I didn't allocate at
least a little bit of time.

00:53:38.233 --> 00:53:39.934
- 'Cause you went
completely all in.

00:53:39.934 --> 00:53:43.367
- [Sasha] Yeah, I
completely went all in.

00:53:45.000 --> 00:53:49.066
And I was always worried about
people's going to steal.

00:53:49.066 --> 00:53:51.233
Let me tell you something.

00:53:52.800 --> 00:53:54.967
From my personal experience,

00:53:54.967 --> 00:53:57.767
you can slip in a
goddamned business.

00:53:57.767 --> 00:53:58.834
If people want to steal

00:53:58.834 --> 00:53:59.900
they're going to
steal while you're there.

00:53:59.900 --> 00:54:02.600
- Dad, do you
think that, real quick--

00:54:02.600 --> 00:54:03.900
J.R., I'm going to
deviate because I think

00:54:03.900 --> 00:54:06.033
this might help a couple people.

00:54:06.033 --> 00:54:08.433
Do you think that,
I mean it was the biggest thing

00:54:08.433 --> 00:54:10.333
you instilled in me at
fourteen, fifteen, sixteen,

00:54:10.333 --> 00:54:12.800
this fear that
employees were gonna steal.

00:54:12.800 --> 00:54:15.200
It was number one. Right?
- [Sasha] Mhmmm.

00:54:15.200 --> 00:54:17.467
- Do you feel like
that's a complete correlation

00:54:17.467 --> 00:54:20.000
to being in Soviet Russia
where everybody was stealing--

00:54:20.000 --> 00:54:22.967
