00:55:40.266 --> 00:55:41.834
- Oh no, you know what this was?

00:55:41.834 --> 00:55:43.533
This was when she was a senior,

00:55:43.533 --> 00:55:45.033
when she was cheerleading right?

00:55:45.033 --> 00:55:49.233
- [Sasha] Cheerleading, and
they were calling the parents--

00:55:49.233 --> 00:55:50.367
- Like you know the last game

00:55:50.367 --> 00:55:51.467
and the parents
come out with the kids.

00:55:51.467 --> 00:55:52.967
That kind of spiel.

00:55:52.967 --> 00:55:55.033
- My daughter, right Elizabeth,

00:55:55.033 --> 00:55:57.400
and I wasn't there, of course.

00:55:57.400 --> 00:55:59.900
My wife was there with

00:55:59.900 --> 00:56:02.467
my youngest son AJ, right?

00:56:02.467 --> 00:56:04.667
How old he was?

00:56:04.667 --> 00:56:08.200
- He was at the time ten.
- [Sasha] Ten.

00:56:08.200 --> 00:56:12.934
They call up
Mr. and Mrs. Vaynerchuk, right?

00:56:12.934 --> 00:56:15.633
And Tamara had AJ

00:56:15.633 --> 00:56:18.400
and she's dragging
him to the podium

00:56:18.400 --> 00:56:20.367
and he didn't want to go.

00:56:20.367 --> 00:56:25.233
You know, now looking
back, it's, you know...

00:56:25.233 --> 00:56:26.800
- AJ got the
benefit though, a little bit?

00:56:26.800 --> 00:56:28.266
- AJ got the benefit.

00:56:28.266 --> 00:56:29.667
He was the youngest one

00:56:29.667 --> 00:56:34.066
and after so many years
working hard and all that...

00:56:34.066 --> 00:56:35.633
- [Gary] Plus, Gary
being in the business.

00:56:35.633 --> 00:56:36.700
- Plus Gary
being in the business.

00:56:36.700 --> 00:56:39.333
Of course, we have
to give him credit.

00:56:39.333 --> 00:56:43.233
Like he doesn't get enough.

00:56:43.233 --> 00:56:44.834
I start going to his games.

00:56:44.834 --> 00:56:46.000
- [Gary] Which is awesome.

00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:48.767
- Yeah and let me
tell you something.

00:56:48.767 --> 00:56:51.667
You have to allocate and
I don't know percentages.

00:56:51.667 --> 00:56:55.133
I don't know how
much time but you have to.

00:56:55.133 --> 00:56:58.100
Listen, I'm
giving a lot of credit

00:56:58.100 --> 00:57:03.000
to my daughter-in-law,
Elizabeth, as well.

00:57:03.000 --> 00:57:07.367
She makes Gary spend
time with kids on the weekend.

00:57:07.367 --> 00:57:08.834
- [Gary] A hundred percent.

00:57:08.834 --> 00:57:12.467
- And you know what, in the
beginning I was kind of eh.

00:57:12.467 --> 00:57:15.867
It was foreign to me
and then I said to myself,

00:57:15.867 --> 00:57:20.033
it's very important and
that's the right thing to do.

00:57:22.166 --> 00:57:27.033
- J.R., are you having a
problem with yourself internally

00:57:27.033 --> 00:57:29.567
or with your partner?

00:57:29.567 --> 00:57:31.500
- [J.R.] Eh,
it's a little bit of both.

00:57:31.500 --> 00:57:35.633
Mainly it's me internally
kinda feeling guilty about it.

00:57:35.633 --> 00:57:38.033
I guess just trying to
get through the hard times,

00:57:38.033 --> 00:57:40.400
if there's maybe a
piece of advice that you have,

00:57:40.400 --> 00:57:42.900
just getting through that guilt.

00:57:42.900 --> 00:57:47.367
- J.R., you're talking to
two men who have zero guilt

00:57:47.367 --> 00:57:48.867
for putting in the time at work.

00:57:48.867 --> 00:57:50.033
(J.R. laughs)

00:57:50.033 --> 00:57:51.700
I promise you
because I share his DNA,

00:57:51.700 --> 00:57:55.767
there was never one day in
the first 18 years of my life,

00:57:55.767 --> 00:57:56.700
not one day.

00:57:56.700 --> 00:57:59.200
You have to understand,
to my dad's credit,

00:57:59.200 --> 00:58:01.500
we live in 2017 now.

00:58:01.500 --> 00:58:03.033
In 1980 and '90,

00:58:03.033 --> 00:58:05.934
there was no conversation
of work-life balance.

00:58:05.934 --> 00:58:08.533
There was no pressure on the
father to be at the game.

00:58:08.533 --> 00:58:10.934
Some fathers did it but
that wasn't a conversation.

00:58:10.934 --> 00:58:11.934
You never heard of that.

00:58:11.934 --> 00:58:14.700
My dad went
through my entire childhood

00:58:14.700 --> 00:58:17.233
not one day having guilt.

00:58:17.233 --> 00:58:18.433
I promise you that truth.

00:58:18.433 --> 00:58:20.367
- [Sasha] Mhmmm. It's true.
- I know it. I'll tell you why.

00:58:20.367 --> 00:58:21.467
I don't either.

00:58:21.467 --> 00:58:23.667
Yes, I spend way
more time with my kids.

00:58:23.667 --> 00:58:24.834
I'm going there right now.

00:58:24.834 --> 00:58:26.533
Like, me and Tyler are looking
at each other right now.

00:58:26.533 --> 00:58:29.033
He's stressed because 
I have to go do something.

00:58:29.033 --> 00:58:31.133
He's stressed because
I have to go to something

00:58:31.133 --> 00:58:33.533
and I can't be late.
I want to go.

00:58:33.533 --> 00:58:34.934
I don't want to be late and
I'm having so much fun with you

00:58:34.934 --> 00:58:38.000
but I have a kid thing
that I'm going to right now.

00:58:38.000 --> 00:58:42.533
Right now I will go to more
functions at my kid's school

00:58:42.533 --> 00:58:45.633
than my dad did in his career
but I will tell you this:

00:58:45.633 --> 00:58:48.467
If I don't go to
a single other one

00:58:48.467 --> 00:58:51.033
from right now to
my kids graduating,

00:58:51.033 --> 00:58:55.734
I will feel zero guilt because
I know like my dad knows

00:58:55.734 --> 00:58:58.567
that our intent
was in the right place.

00:58:58.567 --> 00:59:02.333
My dad grew up in a
place and in the world,

00:59:02.333 --> 00:59:04.233
and he's old
school for old school.

00:59:04.233 --> 00:59:07.533
My dad's 63 going
on 630 in his demeanor.

00:59:07.533 --> 00:59:09.266
He's old school. Right?

00:59:09.266 --> 00:59:10.700
- Yeah, I'm old
school, a handshake.

00:59:10.700 --> 00:59:11.700
- [Gary] Yeah, a
handshake, right?

00:59:11.700 --> 00:59:12.667
- Right.

00:59:12.667 --> 00:59:17.066
- So J.R., you have to
understand, my dad felt no guilt

00:59:17.066 --> 00:59:18.734
and I'll tell you why, J.R.

00:59:18.734 --> 00:59:22.867
He judged himself within himself

00:59:22.867 --> 00:59:26.266
and if he knew his intent
was to provide for the family

00:59:26.266 --> 00:59:28.400
and that was his role,

00:59:28.400 --> 00:59:31.900
especially when he
knew his wife was way better

00:59:31.900 --> 00:59:34.867
at emotional intelligence
and raising the kids,

00:59:34.867 --> 00:59:36.700
and he was better
at doing the thing,

00:59:36.700 --> 00:59:37.934
and I feel the same way.

00:59:37.934 --> 00:59:40.133
I know that everything I decide,

00:59:40.133 --> 00:59:42.333
I'm trying with
the best of my ability.

00:59:42.333 --> 00:59:44.900
J.R., you have to
try the best you can.

00:59:44.900 --> 00:59:46.900
You can't let the outside world,

00:59:46.900 --> 00:59:49.667
not Sasha or Gary Vaynerchuk,
not your partner,

00:59:49.667 --> 00:59:52.500
not your parents,
not a magazine,

00:59:52.500 --> 00:59:54.800
not a podcast, judge you.

00:59:54.800 --> 00:59:56.700
You just have to
do the best you can.

00:59:56.700 --> 00:59:57.834
- Mhmmm.

01:00:00.233 --> 01:00:02.066
Did we
answer your question?

01:00:02.066 --> 01:00:04.700
- [J.R.] Cool. Thank you guys.
